SUMMARY:Beauty and the Beast (1978) | Underground Film Series
DESCRIPTION:The most uncanny and fierce adaptation of Beauty and the Beas
 t\, the film follows the innocent Julie and her experiences living under 
 the watchful eye of Netvor\, a bird-like being torn between his growing a
 ffection for her and his animalistic urge to kill. Directed by Juraj Herz
  of the Czech New Wave\, Herz masterfully infuses the 18th-century French
  fairytale of impossible affection with the aesthetics of gothic horror. 
 Restored by Národní filmový archiv\, Prague and Severin Films\, suppor
 ted by The Czech Audiovisual Fund. [91 min\; horror\, fantasy\; Czech wit
 h English subtitles]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The most uncanny and fierce adaptation 
 of <i>Beauty and the Beast</i>\, the film follows the innocent Julie and 
 her experiences living under the watchful eye of Netvor\, a bird-like bei
 ng torn between his growing affection for her and his animalistic urge to
  kill. Directed by Juraj Herz of the Czech New Wave\, Herz masterfully in
 fuses the 18th-century French fairytale of impossible affection with the 
 aesthetics of gothic horror. Restored by Národní filmový archiv\, Prag
 ue and Severin Films\, supported by The Czech Audiovisual Fund. [91 min\;
  horror\, fantasy\; Czech with English subtitles]</p>
