SUMMARY:The Christophers | Art and a Movie
DESCRIPTION:Julian Sklar (Ian McKellen) was once a star of London's 1960s
  and '70s pop art explosion\, but he hasn't painted in decades and has be
 en broke for years. His two estranged children (James Corden\, Jessica Gu
 nning)\, desperate for an inheritance\, hire Lori\, an art restorer and f
 ormer forger (Michaela Coel)\, to pose as a prospective assistant in orde
 r to access eight unfinished canvases Julian has buried deep in storage. 
 Her plan is to complete them\, then return them to storage\, where they a
 re to be "discovered" upon Julian's death. [100 min\; comedy\, drama\; En
 glish]This program is presented in partnership with the Eskenazi Museum o
 f Art. After the screening\, continue the conversation at the Eskenazi Mu
 seum of Art with a special program led by Jean Graves\, Meier Chair of Ed
 ucation\, focused on how objects in the museum&#8217\;s collections have 
 been affected by conservators\, restorers\, assistants\, and the original
  artists themselves. Register for this free event here.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Julian Sklar (Ian McKellen) was once a 
 star of London's 1960s and '70s pop art explosion\, but he hasn't painted
  in decades and has been broke for years. His two estranged children (Jam
 es Corden\, Jessica Gunning)\, desperate for an inheritance\, hire Lori\,
  an art restorer and former forger (Michaela Coel)\, to pose as a prospec
 tive assistant in order to access eight unfinished canvases Julian has bu
 ried deep in storage. Her plan is to complete them\, then return them to 
 storage\, where they are to be "discovered" upon Julian's death. [100 min
 \; comedy\, drama\; English]</p><p><i><strong>This program is presented i
 n partnership with the Eskenazi Museum of Art. After the screening\, cont
 inue the conversation at the Eskenazi Museum of Art with a special progra
 m led by Jean Graves\, Meier Chair of Education\, focused on how objects 
 in the museum&#8217\;s collections have been affected by conservators\, r
 estorers\, assistants\, and the original artists themselves. Register for
  this free event </strong></i><a class="external" href="https://events.iu
 .edu/bloomington/event/2457787-art-a-movie-at-the-eskenazi-museum-unfinis
 hed-busine"><i><strong>here</strong></i></a><i><strong>.</strong></i></p>
