SUMMARY:The Ballad of Suzanne Cesaire | New Americas Cinema
DESCRIPTION:Based on the life of writer and feminist activist Suzanne Cé
 saire\, Madeleine Hunt-Ehrlich's debut feature explores the relationships
  with Césaire's husband\, French politician Aimé Césaire\, and fellow 
 surrealist André Breton. Shimmering with the radiance of its Caribbean l
 andscape and a phenomenal performance from Zita Hanrot\, the film breaks 
 from traditional biographical structure\, blending more conventional narr
 ative with captivating experimental elements. [75 min\; biography\, drama
 \; English and French with English subtitles]
