SUMMARY:SNEAK PREVIEW: Ink | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:SNEAK PREVIEW SCREENING! See Danny Boyle's acclaimed biopic o
 f media magnate Rupert Murdoch before it's available anywhere.          I
 n November 1969\, 30-something outcast British journalist Larry Lamb (Jac
 k O'Connell—Sinners\; 28 Years Later) met a young Australian media baro
 n named Rupert Murdoch (Guy Pearce—Memento\; L.A. Confidential\; The Br
 utalist) and a partnership began that changed the face of the news foreve
 r. In the London of that era\, the media had its home on the iconic Fleet
  Street\, a hotbed of betrayal\, backstabbing\, and bad behavior\, where 
 it was ruled by the establishment. Lamb and Murdoch took a different appr
 oach\, publishing editions of The Sun loaded with lurid headlines and out
 landish puns\, and covering everything from sports to television to sex\,
  pushing ethical concerns to the sidelines\, and revolutionizing the medi
 a landscape. This is the period that Academy Award-winning director Danny
  Boyle's (Slumdog Millionaire\; 28 Days Later\; Trainspotting\; 28 Years 
 Later) film—written by James Graham\, whose original stage play INK won
  awards on both sides of the Atlantic—covers\, one that saw a successio
 n of firsts that would alter the trajectory of today's 24/7\, clickbait n
 ews landscape and take Lamb and Murdoch down a dark path. [116 min\; dram
 a\; English]        Special thanks to our friends at Netflix for providin
 g this advance access screening.
