SUMMARY:The Plague | Arthouse Now
DESCRIPTION:At all-boys water polo camp\, a 12-year-old boy is pulled int
 o a cruel tradition called The Plague\, which targets an outcast with an 
 "illness." As the lines between game and reality blur\, he fears the joke
  may be hiding something real. IndieWire's Critics' Pic\; Official Select
 ion of the Cannes Film Festival\; Fantastic Fest Best Picture Winner\; no
 minated for Best Feature\, Best Lead Performance\, and Best Breakthrough 
 Performance at the 2025 Independent Spirit Awards. [98 min\; drama\, thri
 ller\; English]
