SUMMARY:The Great Arch | Arthouse Now
DESCRIPTION:1983. French President Mitterrand decides to launch an intern
 ational architectural competition for the flagship project of his mandate
 : the Great Arch of La Défense\, aligned with the Louvre and the Arc de 
 Triomphe. Against all odds\, Otto von Spreckelsen\, a Danish architect\, 
 wins the competition. Overnight\, this 53-year-old man\, unknown in Franc
 e\, arrives in Paris where he is propelled to the helm of this pharaonic 
 project. While the architect intends to build the Great Arch exactly as h
 e envisioned\, his ideas quickly clash with realistic constraints and the
  vicissitudes of politics. [104 min\; drama\; English\, French\, and Dutc
 h with English subtitles]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  1983. French President Mitterrand decid
 es to launch an international architectural competition for the flagship 
 project of his mandate: the Great Arch of La Défense\, aligned with the 
 Louvre and the Arc de Triomphe. Against all odds\, Otto von Spreckelsen\,
  a Danish architect\, wins the competition. Overnight\, this 53-year-old 
 man\, unknown in France\, arrives in Paris where he is propelled to the h
 elm of this pharaonic project. While the architect intends to build the G
 reat Arch exactly as he envisioned\, his ideas quickly clash with realist
 ic constraints and the vicissitudes of politics. [104 min\; drama\; Engli
 sh\, French\, and Dutch with English subtitles]</p>
